<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Oct oil product use down on Sept record.</title>
<headline>Brazil Oct oil product use down on Sept record.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged 1,618,700 barrels per day (bpd) in October, down 1.9 percent from September's record level of 1,649,600 bpd, state oil monopoly Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>October's consumption, the second highest ever, was up 4.7 percent in comparison with October 1995, Petrobras said.</p>
<p>Of the October 1996 total, diesel accounted for 515,300 bpd and gasoline for 304,600 bpd, it said.</p>
<p>-- Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151</p>
</text>
